=You are an AEO schema engineer.

MY NICHE: REPLACE_ME (e.g. n8n + AEO for B2B agencies).
MY TONE: Direct, plain English, no marketing fluff.

Given this post, write 6 FAQ pairs that match how real users phrase their questions to ChatGPT / Perplexity / Google AIO. Ground every answer in the post body — do not invent stats. Answers should be 40-80 words, scannable, and rich in entity language.

POST TITLE: {{ $json.title.rendered }}
POST URL: {{ $json.link }}
POST CONTENT (HTML, stripped to first 6000 chars):
{{ $json.content.rendered.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 6000) }}

Return ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "faqs": [
    {"q": "...", "a": "..."},
    {"q": "...", "a": "..."},
    {"q": "...", "a": "..."},
    {"q": "...", "a": "..."},
    {"q": "...", "a": "..."},
    {"q": "...", "a": "..."}
  ]
}

parameters.jsCode:
const raw = $input.first().json.content?.[0]?.text || $input.first().json.text || '';
const match = raw.match(/\{[\s\S]*\}/);
if (!match) throw new Error('No JSON in Claude reply');
const { faqs } = JSON.parse(match[0]);
if (!Array.isArray(faqs) || faqs.length < 3) throw new Error('Need at least 3 FAQ pairs');

const post = $('WP - fetch post').first().json;

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(f => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: f.a
    }
  }))
};

// Quick validation
for (const item of schema.mainEntity) {
  if (!item.name || !item.acceptedAnswer.text) {
    throw new Error('Empty FAQ field — refusing to write');
  }
}

return [{
  json: {
    post_id: post.id,
    post_title: post.title.rendered,
    post_url: post.link,
    faqs,
    schema_jsonld: JSON.stringify(schema),
    injected_at: new Date().toISOString()
  }
}];

